  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed in both technical/industrial and medical contexts. In medicine, ⟦{動脈|どうみゃく}→動脈：05857_doumyaku⟧{硬化|こうか} (arteriosclerosis) is the most well-known compound. In manufacturing and construction, it refers to the curing or hardening of materials.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{動脈|どうみゃく}→動脈：05857_doumyaku⟧{硬化|こうか}: arteriosclerosis\n- {硬化|こうか}{剤|ざい}: hardening agent, curing agent\n- {硬化|こうか}⟦コンクリート→コンクリート：10858_konkuriito⟧: hardened concrete\n- ⟦{表面|ひょうめん}→表面：03587_hyoumen⟧{硬化|こうか}: surface hardening",
